            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation and management of pain in autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e1-e16</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.ackd.2010.01.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Transient episodes of pain are common in autosomal dominant polycystic kidney disease (ADPKD). A small fraction of patients have disabling chronic pain. In this review, we discuss the etiologies of pain in ADPKD; review how ADPKD patients should be assessed; and discuss medical, surgical, and other management options.</AbstractText>
